## What to Look For in an Android TV Remote App

### Must-Have Features

- **Reliable auto-discovery** — You shouldn't need to type IP addresses
- **Low latency** — Control should feel instant, not sluggish
- **Full keyboard** — Essential for searching on YouTube, Netflix, etc.
- **D-pad and media controls** — The basics that every remote needs

### Nice-to-Have Features

- **Touchpad mode** — Useful for navigating web browser apps on TV
- **Customizable layout** — Rearrange buttons to suit your habits
- **OLED dark theme** — Saves battery, looks great in a dark room
- **No ads** — Especially important for nighttime use

### Red Flags to Avoid

- Interstitial ads between actions
- Required account creation just to use the remote
- Vague or absent privacy policies
- No GitHub or public repository link

